# wren_engine — Feedback Engine RUNTIME dependency manifest.
#
# Unlike requirements.in (TEST-ONLY tooling for the whole wren_engine package),
# this file lists the RUNTIME dependencies of ONLY the Feedback Engine's model
# invocation path (wren_engine/model_invocation.py, Task 9.3). The Diff Engine,
# Anchor Service, and Progress Tracker remain pure standard-library logic with
# zero runtime dependencies and are NOT affected by this file.
#
# design.md: "Feedback_Engine, Feedback_Presenter (data) | Feedback Engine
# container Lambda | Python 3.12 | Heavy AI workload; `langchain-aws`, larger
# deps -> container image" — this manifest is bundled into that container
# image only, never into the lightweight Diff/Anchor/Progress Lambda(s).
#
# Model invocation is model-agnostic (REQ-NFR-MODEL-01): langchain-aws's
# ChatBedrockConverse accepts any Bedrock model id as a runtime string: no
# model-specific package is added when the configured model id changes.
#
# Versions verified against PyPI release metadata: langchain-aws==1.0.0
# requires langchain-core>=1.0.0 and boto3>=1.40.19; pinned below to the
# latest releases satisfying those constraints at the time of writing.
langchain-aws==1.0.0
langchain-core==1.4.9
boto3==1.40.63
